  "description": "The robotic bark: a metallic ring-modulated square over a clean sine sub that snaps open and rolls off on every triplet eighth, swinging against straight-eighth drum patterns. Play: short F1, G1 and A#1 stabs or held notes at 140-150 BPM; the ring-mod pitch follows your keys, so melodic lines stay metallic but in tune with the sub. Macros: Bark sets how far the timbre falls on each triplet, Metal deepens the ring modulation, Snap sharpens the notch sweep and Drive pushes the diode distortion.",
